  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_1",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_SpearPhishing-Targeting-Mongolian-Government(02-22-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s1"
      },
      "text": "FireEye recently observed a sophisticated campaign targeting individuals within the Mongolian government.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_2",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_SpearPhishing-Targeting-Mongolian-Government(02-22-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s2"
      },
      "text": "Targeted individuals that enabled macros in a malicious Microsoft Word document may have been infected with Poison Ivy , a popular remote access tool (RAT) that has been used for nearly a decade for key logging, screen and video capture, file transfers, password theft, system administration, traffic relaying, and more.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_9",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_SpearPhishing-Targeting-Mongolian-Government(02-22-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s9"
      },
      "text": "The threat actors used two publicly available techniques, an AppLocker whitelisting bypass and a script to inject shellcode into the userinit.exe process.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_14",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_SpearPhishing-Targeting-Mongolian-Government(02-22-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s2"
      },
      "text": "In April 2016, a security researcher demonstrated a way to bypass this using regsvr32.exe, a legitimate Microsoft executable permitted to execute in many AppLocker policies.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_20",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_SpearPhishing-Targeting-Mongolian-Government(02-22-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s3"
      },
      "text": "There was code to download a decoy document from the Internet and open it in a second winword.exe process using the Start-Process cmdlet.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_22",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_SpearPhishing-Targeting-Mongolian-Government(02-22-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s1"
      },
      "text": "After launching the decoy document in the second winword.exe process, the PowerShell script downloads and runs another PowerShell script named f0921.ps1 as shown in Figure 7.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_27",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_SpearPhishing-Targeting-Mongolian-Government(02-22-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 8,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p8_s1"
      },
      "text": "After the shellcode is decrypted and run, it injects a Poison Ivy backdoor into the userinit.exe as shown in Figure 14.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_28",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_SpearPhishing-Targeting-Mongolian-Government(02-22-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 9,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p9_s1"
      },
      "text": "In the decrypted shellcode, we also observed content and configuration related to Poison Ivy.",
      "language": "en",
